// Milestone — the curated question library. INPUT to scripts/geography/build-milestones.mjs.
//
// One entry per question:
//   id     stable id (never reuse or rename — saved games refer to it)
//   cat    science · invention · firsts · history · exploration · engineering · sport ·
//          culture · archaeology · nature
//   year   when it happened (shown as a chip; negative = BCE)
//   q      the clue. Never names the answer place.
//   a      the answer, as the reveal names it; `place` = where that is
//   site   English Wikipedia article for the exact spot. Its coordinates become the
//          answer; `ll` is our own reading of them, and the builder fails if the two
//          disagree by more than max(25 km, 2r) — so a wrong article can't slip through.
//   v      the opening view: a named region (VIEWS) or an explicit [lat, lon, zoom],
//          zoom = world width ÷ view width. Chosen per question: wide enough to reason
//          in, never centred on the answer.
//   r      scoring precision in km: full 1,000 inside r, then decaying (see postcard.js
//          scoring notes / milestone.js). Small for a single building or field, larger
//          for an event spread over a region.
//   d      difficulty 1–3 (the daily runs easy → hard)
//   why    the explanation shown after the guess
//   refs   further Wikipedia articles used to check the claim
//
// Careful distinctions are written into the clues: discovered vs published, invented vs
// patented vs demonstrated, event vs birthplace. Anything with a genuinely disputed
// location is left out.

